---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Disclaimer" description="Legal disclaimer for Decent Investing.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-12 pt-16 sm:px-6">
    <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
      <em>Last updated: October 2026</em>
    </p>

    <h2>Not Professional Advice</h2>
    <p>
      The content provided on this website is for <strong
        >informational and educational purposes only</strong
      >
      and should not be construed as professional financial, investment, tax, or legal advice. The author
      is not a licensed financial adviser, does not hold an Australian financial services (AFS) licence,
      is not a New Zealand financial advice provider, and is not a registered tax agent.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>General information only.</strong> This guide doesn't take into account your objectives,
      financial situation or needs. Before acting on it, consider whether it's appropriate for you.
    </p>

    <h2>No Fiduciary Relationship</h2>
    <p>
      Reading or using this information does not establish a professional-client or fiduciary
      relationship. The strategies discussed may not be suitable for your specific financial
      situation, risk tolerance, or goals.
    </p>

    <h2>Risk Warning</h2>
    <p>
      Investing involves risk, including the <strong>potential loss of principal</strong>. Past
      performance of any security or strategy is not a guarantee of future results. Financial
      markets are volatile and subject to fluctuation.
    </p>

    <h2>Accuracy and Currency</h2>
    <p>
      While every effort has been made to ensure the accuracy of the information at the time of
      writing, tax laws, investment regulations, contribution limits, and market conditions change
      frequently.
    </p>
    <p>
      Specific dollar figures (contribution limits, income thresholds) are noted with the year they
      apply to. <strong>Always verify current-year numbers</strong> at authoritative sources:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Australian super caps and rates: <a
          href="https://www.ato.gov.au/tax-rates-and-codes/key-superannuation-rates-and-thresholds"
          >ato.gov.au</a
        > (changes each 1 July)
      </li>
      <li>
        Australian money guidance: <a href="https://moneysmart.gov.au/">moneysmart.gov.au</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        KiwiSaver and NZ tax: <a href="https://www.ird.govt.nz/kiwisaver">ird.govt.nz</a> (changes each
        1 April)
      </li>
      <li>New Zealand money guidance: <a href="https://sorted.org.nz/">sorted.org.nz</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Fund References</h2>
    <p>
      References to specific investment products (such as VGS, VAS, IOZ, DHHF, VDHG, Smart TWF and
      Simplicity funds) are used as <strong>examples, not recommendations</strong>. Comparable
      low-cost funds are available from other providers. Fees change; check the provider's current
      product disclosure statement. The author has no financial relationship with any fund provider
      mentioned.
    </p>

    <h2>Consult a Professional</h2>
    <p>
      You should consult with a qualified financial adviser, tax agent or accountant, or lawyer
      before making any significant financial decisions. In Australia, check the adviser is on the
      <a href="https://moneysmart.gov.au/financial-advice/financial-advisers-register"
        >Financial Advisers Register</a
      >. In New Zealand, check they're on the
      <a href="https://fsp-register.companiesoffice.govt.nz/"
        >Financial Service Providers Register</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong
        >You are solely responsible for your own financial decisions and the consequences thereof.</strong
      >
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
